script:pre-request {
  if (!bru.getVar("baseUrl")) bru.setVar("baseUrl", "http://localhost:3000/api/v1");
}

docs {
  # Edge Cases in TAT (NABL feature)

  Every edge case from Master/NABL-TAT-QA-TESTING.md as a runnable Bruno flow.

  ## How to run
  1. **Run Folder** on **00 Base Setup** first (in the same Bruno session). It
     runs the complete API flow and seeds the shared variables (operatorToken,
     branchId, branchLabTestId, labReportId, sampleId, orderId). It leaves NABL
     TAT OFF.
  2. Open an **EC## <case>** folder and Run/Send its requests in order. Each case
     folder switches NABL on/off and sets the processing window for that case,
     then verifies.

  ## Mutating vs observing
  Requests named Enable/Disable/Set Window/Approve/Cancel CHANGE data. After a
  mutating case (Approve/Cancel), re-run 00 Base Setup before the next case so it
  starts from a clean report/order. Verify (GET) requests are safe to repeat.

  ## Timing
  The NABL clock is driven by a 1-minute cron and the wall clock vs the window.
  Cases that need the clock to actually start/pause/resume tell you to wait ~1
  minute (or until the window edge / next day) and re-send, and to confirm the
  lab_reports columns in the DB (is_nabl_tat, tat_is_running, tat_start_at,
  tat_net_minutes, tat_end_at). The pure calculation logic behind every case is
  also covered by unit tests (nabl-tat-stopwatch.util.spec.ts, branch-open.util.spec.ts).
}
